{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The wife of Moses.</b> She is mentioned by the name of her husband, for he was a king." "<b>After he had sent her away.</b> Were it not for this verse, we would not have known that Moses sent her away, but would have thought she was with him, as it is written: 'וירכיבם על החמור' (and he set them upon the donkey). Now it comes and teaches you here: when Aaron and Moses and Israel met, they were steeped in distress, while Jethro was in comfort — so he sent her away."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:23.775560855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}